{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T11:33:53.568Z","author":"pm-github","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.2-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"4400fc26dce6d999aa811cc5","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.2-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"The pm-github importer and reusable workflow changes are tracked in #287. The published 2026.11.26 package still reproduces the pm-rl repeat failure. The merged #288 comment fix landed after that tag, and its built code preserves item and history bytes against the same frozen source.\n\nAfter a release includes the fixes, update the reusable workflow pin and installed extension together in pm-rl, pm-web, pm-vcs, and pm-hypothesis. Record the exact caller and reusable workflow SHAs, installed extension version, and hosted run URL for each caller. Confirm that apply and repeat succeed with unchanged issue evidence and that a source change stops the run before branch publication. Preserve the existing privacy and repeat-diff gates.\n\nReported caller failures are documented in [pm-rl #210](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/issues/210), [pm-web #369](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/issues/369), the [pm-vcs repeat run](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/45801461445), and [pm-hypothesis #61](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-hypothesis/issues/61). The pm-rl reproduction identified a duplicate long comment. The other callers still need independent hosted verification."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-github-github-ee4d59c27b67-297"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Roll out and verify repeat-import recovery in four gated sync callers"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH issue #297: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/issues/297 · author @unbraind · created 2026-11-27T11:32:22Z · updated